# Dependencies
node_modules/
# package-lock.json is intentionally COMMITTED: `npm ci` requires it, and it is
# what makes dependency resolution reproducible between local, CI, and Vercel.

# Environment
# Ignore every .env variant by default. The previous list named only .env,
# .env.local, and .env.production, which left files like .env.stage and
# .env.vercel committable — both had in fact been committed (with empty values).
.env*
!.env.example

# Non-dotfile env dumps. `env.txt` was committed in fdb8ea9 carrying live
# RESOLVER_PRIVATE_KEY, BASE_SEPOLIA_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY and
# MEZO_TESTNET_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY values; deleting the file in 767c620 did not
# remove them from history. These names must never be committable again.
env.txt
ENV_EXAMPLE.txt
*env*.txt
*.key
*_PRIVATE_KEY*

